saturating-time 0.5.0: stop find_limit() spinning forever on Windows.

Windows SystemTime counts in 100 ns ticks, and checked_sub()/checked_add()
with a step under 100 ns returns Some(the same value) instead of None, so the
search for SystemTime's minimum never ends and Arti's first consensus parse
hangs (https://github.com/solardev-xyz/freedom-browser/issues/925).

This is upstream's fix, verbatim: Arti MR 4520,
https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/arti/-/merge_requests/4520
(commit e168fab8bc49e7a81a567a04b5dd04abb4ce7e5d). Applied by
scripts/fetch-arti.js to the crates.io saturating-time 0.5.0 source, Windows
builds only. Remove it once a released Arti ships the fix:
https://github.com/solardev-xyz/freedom-browser/issues/926

--- a/src/internal.rs
+++ b/src/internal.rs
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 static MIN_INSTANT: LazyLock<Instant> = LazyLock::new(find_min);
 
 /// An internal trait implementing the actual magic behind this.
-pub trait SaturatingTime: Sized + Copy {
+pub trait SaturatingTime: Sized + Copy + PartialEq {
     /// Anchor method to obtain an instance of this type.
     fn anchor() -> Self;
 
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@
 /// 1. Set `step` to `INITIAL_STEP` and `res` to [`SaturatingTime::anchor()`].
 /// 2. Call `f(&res, step)`.
 ///     1. If [`Some`], set `res` to the returned value and continue.
+///         * A [`Some`] that is equal to the previous value is considered as a
+///           [`None`] due to a long lived bug in the Rust standard library.
 ///     2. If [`None`] and `step == 1ns`, return `res`.
 ///     3. Else, set `step` to `MAX{1ns, step / 2}` and continue.
 fn find_limit<T, F>(f: F) -> T
@@ -142,11 +144,12 @@
         // (2) Call f().
         let next = f(&res, step);
         match next {
-            Some(st) => {
+            // We only consider a Some as a Some if the value actually changed.
+            Some(st) if st != res => {
                 // (2.1) If Some, set res to the returned value and continue.
                 res = st;
             }
-            None => {
+            None | Some(_) => {
                 if step == ONE_NS {
                     // (2.2) If None and step == 1ns, return res.
                     return res;
